Flashnack is a web port of LoFi Logic (flashback-raw-editor),
https://github.com/lofilogic/flashback-raw-editor, made by LoFi Logic and
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3. Flashnack is
licensed under the same licence; see LICENSE.

Ported from LoFi Logic (GPL-3.0), each file says what it came from and what
changed:
  - the colour pipeline: ForwardMatrix, highlight recovery, white balance and
    tint, ACEScct, tone curves, V1 negative develop (core/processor.py,
    core/v1_negative.py, core/config.py)
  - every render stage and its order (core/processor.py, core/effects.py,
    core/kernels.py, core/gpu.py)
  - the WGSL compute shaders in src/gpu/shaders, copied unchanged apart from a
    header (core/shaders)
  - the five looks and their settings (core/config.py VIBE_PRESETS)
  - the 3D LUTs in public/luts, converted from assets/luts/*.cube to binary
  - the film grain tiles in public/grain (assets/grain)
  - export file names (core/export_naming.py)

Flashnack is not affiliated with LoFi Logic or with Flashback (joinflashback.co).
"Flashback" and "ONE35" are names of Flashback's camera products, used here only
to say which files Flashnack opens.

